@title How a building permit application is routed
@subtitle Whitcombe City planning office
@date 2026-10-01

## Routing flow

diagram permit dir=TB title="Permit routing"
permit: start "Application received" svc focus
permit: complete "Submission complete?" decision
permit: ret "Return to applicant" ext
permit: value "Project value over 50000 dollars?" decision
permit: fast "Fast-track review" svc
permit: hist "In a historic district?" decision
permit: heritage "Heritage Board review" team
permit: plan "Plan review" svc
permit: issued "Permit issued" svc focus
permit: start -> complete
permit: complete -> ret : no
permit: complete -> value : yes
permit: value -> fast : no
permit: value -> hist : yes
permit: hist -> heritage : yes
permit: hist -> plan : no
permit: heritage -> plan : cleared
permit: fast -> issued : approved
permit: plan -> issued : approved

## Review times

table = stage,target; Completeness check,within 2 business days; Fast-track review,within 3 business days; Plan review,within 15 business days; Heritage Board review,within 30 days

! Heritage Board review time is added on top of the plan review time.

## Fees

kpi Base fee | $180 | every application
kpi Value fee | 0.8% | of the project value above $50,000

Every application pays the base fee of $180, plus 0.8% of the project value above $50,000.
